Package: genmetalite
Type: Package
Title: Generalized Meta-Analysis of Reduced Regression Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emily", "Norton", email = "mlenorton@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Combines coefficient estimates from several studies that each fit a
    "reduced" regression model containing only a subset of the covariates in a
    target "full" model. Following the generalized meta-analysis framework, the
    reduced-model coefficients are mapped onto the full-model parameter using
    covariate second moments borrowed from an external reference population, and
    the mapped estimates are pooled by generalized least squares. Variance
    estimation uses an influence-function sandwich that propagates uncertainty
    from the reference sample and, when covariance blocks are taken from the
    studies themselves, from the study samples. The reference population may be
    reweighted to resemble each study by entropy balancing or inverse
    probability weighting, and complex-survey reference samples (stratified,
    clustered designs such as NHANES) are supported. Inverse-variance weighted
    and empirical-Bayes style pooled estimators are provided for comparison.
